[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/EDGEbuilder/main/packs/remove-doors/nexus/brand/banner.png[/img][/center]

[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Take any door out of Night City, and put it back whenever you like.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]Remove Doors is a small app for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url]. It lists the doors near V, outlines them in the game, and removes the one you pick from the world, so the doorway is open and V walks through. Removed doors stay removed in every save while the app is on. Bring one back with a click, or switch the app off and they all come back.[/size][/center]

[center][size=3]Guide: [url=https://edgemodders.ai/wiki/edgebuilder/remove-doors.html]Remove Doors in the wiki[/url] · Made by the team behind [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/36627]EDGEbuilder[/url][/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What it does[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Doors near V.[/b] Every door within 30 m, nearest first, with whether it is open, closed or locked. A switch each for working doors (apartments, elevators, shutters) and painted-on doors (the ones that never open).[/*]
[*][b]See which is which.[/b] [b]Show all[/b] outlines every listed door in the game; the door you pick gets a red outline.[/*]
[*][b]Remove.[/b] The door goes, with the stand-in copy the game draws of it from afar, so the doorway is really open.[/*]
[*][b]Kept.[/b] Removed doors stay removed after loading a save, in every save, while the app is on.[/*]
[*][b]Bring back.[/b] Each removed door has [b]Bring back[/b], and [b]Bring all back[/b] returns them all. Switching the app off in REDnode's Mod Manager does the same.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] 0.67.3 or later, with what it needs (RED4ext, redscript).[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/7780]Codeware[/url] 1.14 or later.[/*]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, [b]game version 2.5[/b].[/*]
[/list]
Nothing else: no REDbridge, no project, and no files written into your game.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] Mod Manager Download, then enable and deploy. Install REDnode first.[/*]
[*][b]EDGEdeck:[/b] Add mod, pick the zip, Deploy.[/*]
[*][b]By hand:[/b] extract the zip into the game folder, so the app lands in [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/remove-doors/[/i].[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]First run[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Start the game. Press [b]F10[/b] for the REDnode launcher, open the [b]Mod Manager[/b], select [b]Remove Doors[/b], switch it on and pin it to the launcher. Do this before you load a save: the app needs to see the world load.[/*]
[*]Load a save and walk up to a door. The [b]Remove Doors[/b] window lists the doors near V.[/*]
[*]Press [b]Pick[/b] next to one: it gets a red outline. Press [b]Remove[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Good to know[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Missions.[/b] Removing a door a mission opens, locks or walks you through can break that mission, or let V into places that aren't finished. Bring it back if a mission stops.[/*]
[*][b]A door brought back after a load[/b] shows as its stand-in, which doesn't open, until the area loads again: fast travel away and back, or load a save.[/*]
[*][b]Started after a save loaded?[/b] The app says so: load the save again, or fast travel, and it can remove doors.[/*]
[*][b]To make it part of your own mod[/b], for anyone who installs it, use [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/36627]EDGEbuilder[/url]: its bake keeps removed doors removed without any app running.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Shout outs[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]The Cyberpunk 2077 modding community: RED4ext, redscript, Codeware and ArchiveXL, and RED Hot Tools, whose world inspector showed how the game's world can be read.[/*]
[/list]
